+++ b/tools/experiments/vnext/source_census/HOST-STATUS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@
+# Source-only host and oracle checkpoint
+
+Prepared against the reviewed proposal tree
+`73b5dc67f3b9c0e6104426017b59adcd7939c4c6` (remote checkpoint `383fe844`).
+These four new files have not been compiled or executed. They do not change the
+reviewed `Main.chibi`, README, or ABI header and do not upgrade the proposal's
+acceptance status. Compiler implementation, bridge generation, native linking,
+independent review, actual closure matching, and all native gates remain pending.
+
+## Host boundary
+
+`host.c` is one Linux x86-64 System V AOT executable entry, linked to the actual
+compiled `Census` symbol. It opens one regular file, checks its representable
+extent, allocates once, reads that exact opaque extent, checks EOF and closes the
+file before invoking `Census(pointer, length)`. The storage remains allocated and
+unchanged throughout the call, then is explicitly freed. Empty input uses NULL
+with length zero. Actual allocation plus completed reads establishes storage;
+integer bounds alone cannot establish a foreign pointer's validity.
+
+The foreign hook captures 16 i64 values and returns its status unchanged. After
+return the host checks exactly one callback and return/status agreement. Success
+prints the 16 values in ABI order, separated by spaces. Rejection prints the input
+filename, byte offset, status, and frame extent to stderr. The captured tuple is
+not re-counted or interpreted as a second census. Output errors are separate from
+census rejection, including delayed close failure and a closed output pipe.
+
+Exit codes: 0 success, 1 census rejection, 2 usage, 3 input/environment I/O,
+4 report-call/return contract failure, 5 output I/O. Output failure takes
+precedence over other exit codes. Allocation failure closes owned resources and
+aborts, following repository policy. Reads retry EINTR; Linux close is not
+retried because its descriptor is already consumed. Extent checks detect growth
+or truncation while reading, not same-sized external rewrites or repository
+identity. The owned buffer is immutable during Census regardless of later file
+changes. There is no JIT adapter, frame preparer, sidecar builder, or new runner.
+
+## Oracle and authored controls
+
+`reference.census(bytes_or_readonly_mmap)` returns the same 16-integer tuple.
+Standard little-endian `struct` unpacking follows statuses 1 through 19 in the
+specified order; every failure zeros the 13 counters. Byte LF splitting handles
+physical lines, omits the artificial trailing segment, and carries a boolean
+across bounded chunks. A byte regex recognizes exactly the complement of ASCII
+whitespace 9..13 and 32. No Unicode line/space rules or Chibi byte loop is used.
+
+The CLI maps an already prepared file read-only and prints the tuple even on a
+census error. Its input must remain unchanged while mapped. A mapping is an
+oracle memory tradeoff, not the host's ownership model or a provenance proof.
+
+The ordinary `reference_tests.py` suite covers every named byte-line case,
+multi-package and replacement accounting, field mutation/truncation, package
+reordering, trailing junk, first-error precedence, all small malformed statuses,
+4096/4097 packages, 16384/16385 originals, generated counts 0/1/2 and bytes 256/257.
+Large tests are explicitly selected with `CHIBI_CENSUS_LARGE_TESTS=1` and cover
+statuses 2/13/14, 16 MiB and 256 MiB minus/at/plus one, and full original capacity
+plus the permitted generated record at the exact 268632348-byte frame cap. They
+construct sparse temporary files from record iterators only when executed.
+Neither test set has been run. Default execution skips the large class; it must
+not be reported as full-domain coverage without the explicit large run.
+
+## Source review and cost estimate
+
+- Transform/consumers: one opaque file into one live borrow for compiled Census;
+  exact bytes into a 16-value independent oracle report for later native matching.
+- Minimum host work: O(B) kernel-to-owned-buffer copy, one allocation/free,
+  one Census call and one 128-byte scalar capture. No frame parse or payload
+  census is in C. At the admitted frame cap B is 268632348 bytes; oversized input
+  still needs real storage if passed to Census rather than a forged extent.
+- Oracle work: O(B + R) unpacking, chunk splitting and byte-regex searches, with
+  up to 16385 records. Each chunk is at most 64 KiB, with at most 65537 segment
+  references. Split may copy a chunk once in addition to the chunk slice, but
+  never repeatedly copies a full large payload or retains all frame lines.
+  Object overhead is Python-version dependent and bounded by the chunk, while
+  mapped pages can still occupy up to the whole input's resident size.
+- On the documented historical 3.8 MB frame, native memory work should fit a
+  frame-to-subsecond scale; the independent Python oracle should be on a
+  subsecond-to-seconds scale. At 256 MiB, expect seconds to a minute for dense-LF
+  inputs rather than promise throughput. Actual I/O, regex, Python-loop and resident-memory
+  costs are unknown until measured. This is a cold correctness oracle.
+
+Source inspection found and addressed output SIGPIPE handling, buffered close
+failure, a retained chunk segment list, and avoidable per-record tuple updates.
+No runtime result is claimed. Before acceptance, execute ordinary and full-domain
+tests, compare every report field through real JIT/AOT, test zero/multiple report
+calls and mismatched return, distinct ABI positions, empty/NULL and guard-page
+borrows, host I/O/allocation/close/output failure controls, and minimized fuzz
+replays. Native execution and hostile-pointer testing belong to the coordinating
+gate; forged or freed pointers are not valid safe-rejection tests.
+
+What to delete: no old implementation is replaced by these sources. What to
+measure: the listed unknown costs and native/host failures. What to leave alone:
+the reviewed caller/ABI and repository identity preparation, which needs another
+actual consumer before sharing preparation machinery.
