+# Source implementation checkpoint (not executed)
+
+This worktree is an untested v4 candidate based on verified remote tree
+73b5dc67f3b9c0e6104426017b59adcd7939c4c6. The old detached HEAD and preexisting
+staged changes are not this checkpoint's delta. Compare against that tree.
+
+Model.chibi remains the single authority. TypeKind appends BorrowedBytes=3;
+opcodes append SubI64=12, ByteLength=13, ByteReadChecked=14. Canonical nominal
+and intrinsic descriptors are restricted Model constants/literal functions,
+not new Module tables.
+The retained reader resolves the exact nominal; the backend sees only TypeKind.
+The generator admits restricted zero-argument string-literal functions and
+emits their Rust constant identities. V3 digest/history and generated v3 files are deliberately untouched.
+V4 is NOT in VERSION_LAYOUTS yet: generation fails closed with its candidate
+layout digest until independent review authorizes that digest. There is no
+fallback accepting a v3 packet as v4 and no handwritten generated output.
+
+All ten ordinary record widths stay unchanged, particularly Value=8 and
+Instruction=24 scalar bytes. No per-module descriptor rows or runtime pointers
+are serialized. The planned backend pair rows are 12 bytes per logical borrow;
+this exact caller needs two rows, 24 bytes. Ordinary scalar map slots remain four
+bytes. Caller input owns the allocation for one synchronous invocation.
+
+The active block cap remains 64 until bounded cyclic-verifier tests, parser
+inventory, and 128/129 controls execute. At 64 the v3 derived ceilings remain
+4,364,216 transport payload bytes. At the proposed 128, unchanged row/table
+shapes imply 4096 blocks, 262144 parameters, 270336 values, 12288 instructions,
+8192 edges/calls, 786432 arguments and 7,116,728 transport bytes. These are
+arithmetic ceilings, not capacity reservations or measured layouts.
+
+Named consumers: Produce reads Model descriptors and retained reader results;
+Verify checks canonical values/operations/CFG; generated Pack and Arena carry
+the same rows; define_bodies lowers that Arena twice for JIT and linked-object
+proof; source_census/Main.chibi is the real-byte caller. No production compiler,
+default toolchain, owned_process.py, or run_native.py is changed.
+
+## Required execution and review gates
+
+Nothing in this checkpoint has been compiled, generated, or tested. First review
+the complete delta, then authorize bounded generation: run generate.py once to
+obtain the unreviewed v4 candidate digest, independently inspect/recompute it,
+record that digest in VERSION_LAYOUTS, generate, and run generate.py --check.
+Run generate_tests.py and retained typed/packing preparation tests only after
+review. Compile the exact retained-parser caller and typed mutations under the
+coordinator's existing owned execution fences. Only then consider raising the
+cap to 128 with its own reviewed digest (or fold that change into the first v4
+publication before any v4 acceptance). Do not publish active mismatched bindings.
+
+Native gates remain the source-census README acceptance sequence: guards and
+live allocations including guard pages; distinct sixteen-position JIT/AOT ABI;
+independent CCN1 oracle and malformed limits; actual immutable closure matching;
+all five current public selections; exact-head nine ordered independent reviews.
+Historical v3 proofs accept none of these additions.
+
+## First coherent source checkpoint
+
